    "title": "What we know about the Malcolm in the Middle reboot plot",
    "text": "Stay up to date with notifications from The IndependentNotifications can be managed in browser preferences.Jump to contentThank you for registeringPlease refresh the page or navigate to another page on the site to be automatically logged inPlease refresh your browser to be logged inAllNewsSportCultureLifestyleMalcolm in the Middle: Life's Still Unfair - trailerHulu is premiering a four-part revival of the popular sitcom Malcolm in the Middle, titled Life’s Still Unfair, on Friday. The series sees the return of original cast members including Frankie Muniz as Malcolm, Bryan Cranston, Jane Kaczmarek, Christopher Kennedy Masterson, and Justin Berfield. Set 20 years after the original, Malcolm is now a father to a teenage daughter, Leah, and attempts to protect her from his chaotic family. Original series creator Linwood Boomer and co-producer Tracy Katsky Boomer developed the revival to explore new family dynamics, particularly Malcolm as a parent, rather than for financial gain. The plot revolves around Malcolm's parents' 40th wedding anniversary, which forces the dysfunctional family to reunite, promising both painful and hilarious insights into unchanging family dynamics. In fullMalcolm in the Middle returns after 20 years with its trademark crazinessThank you for registeringPlease refresh the page or navigate to another page on the site to be automatically logged inPlease refresh your browser to be logged in",
